name issue_268_freeze_rule_outage
describe Video-only call, 3 s outage at 10 s: freezes counted as libwebrtc's VideoQualityObserver counts them (issue #268)
# libwebrtc (video/video_quality_observer2.cc, OnRenderedFrame) puts each render interval in the
# 30-frame average before testing it and keeps freezes in it, so the outage raises the threshold
# and the stalls while video recovers are not counted again. Before the fix FreezeDetector left
# freezes out of the average and counted them: seed 1 had 3 freezes, 5282 ms (now 1, 4710 ms);
# seed 4 had 4, 5643 ms (now 2, 5070 ms). Seeds 2, 3 and 5 are the same before and after.
# The unit tests FreezeDetector.* pin libwebrtc's exact counts from sm_video_compare's inputs.
seed 1
duration 40s
audio off
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s down
at 13s up
expect video.frames_rendered > 1000
expect video.freeze_count <= 2
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 5200
